<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/inventions?focus=horse-collar">Inventions &amp; Discoveries</a> · Farming and food</p><h1 class="enc-title">Horse collar</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">late 5th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/5th-century">5th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">A horse collar is a padded harness collar that spreads a load across a horse's shoulders and chest without pressing on its windpipe; it was invented in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> by the early <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">medieval period</a>. The earliest certain depiction is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dunhuang">Dunhuang</a> cave mural of 477–499 CE, from the Northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cao-wei">Wei dynasty</a>. It spread westward and was clearly in use in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a> by 1000, where horses came to be used more widely for ploughing, working roughly 50 per cent faster than oxen.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/horse-collar.jpg" alt="Horse collar" width="320" height="206" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Earliest_equine_harness_477_499_cave_257.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="inv-entry"><h2 class="enc-section-title">On the inventions tree</h2><dl class="inv-entry-facts"><div><dt>First known</dt><dd>477–499 CE</dd></div><div><dt>Where</dt><dd>Dunhuang, China</dd></div></dl><p class="inv-entry-note"><span class="inv-k">Note</span>An earlier, doubtful depiction comes from a 3rd-century tomb in Sichuan, and some see a partial collar in ancient Rome.</p><div class="inv-entry-rel"><span class="inv-k">Built on</span><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/plough">Plough<span>c. 2800 BCE</span></a><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/domestication-of-the-horse">Domestication of the horse<span>c. 2200 BCE</span></a></div><p class="enc-article-foot"><a class="enc-random-link" href="/inventions?focus=horse-collar">See it on the inventions tree &rarr;</a></p></section>
